---
title: Folders
description: Group Muse boards into folders and open them inline on the canvas, without navigating away.
---

Folders group related boards together. Unlike a traditional file tree, a Muse folder can be
**opened inline** on the canvas — its boards expand in place so you can move between them
without losing your spot or your zoom level.

## Creating a folder

Select one or more boards and choose **Group into folder**, or drop a board onto another to
nest it. A folder is itself an object on the canvas, so it has a position and can live inside
another folder.

## Opening inline

Clicking a folder expands it in place rather than routing to a new page. The folder's boards
fan out around it; collapsing returns them to the folder object. This keeps navigation
spatial — you stay on one continuous surface.

## Where folders are stored

A folder is structured data, not media, so it persists to the
[queryable layer](/docs/neoworks/openschema) on your NeoWorks account and syncs like any other
board. See [Sync & data](/docs/muse/sync) for the details.
